  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to Integrated Border and Migration Management in Libya - First Phase</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of this IOM project is to strengthen the capacity of relevant Libyan authorities in south Libya to manage national borders and mixed migration flows more efficiently and in compliance with international human rights law. IOM will apply the concept of humanitarian border management, which includes evaluating large-scale cross-border migratory flows to develop border management procedures and contingency plans for emergencies, natural and/or anthropogenic crisis situations. This will be complemented by support to pandemic management measures to human mobility management under the framework of health, border and mobility management.</narrative>
  </description>
